35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Shizue, I found that supervised mornings are short, and neighbors already refuse to turn bags away. We can keep talking without stress!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, that is kind of you. I found our log shows many complaints from one gate, and the station block argued over sweeping. We must be gentle.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, the truck arrives between seven forty and eight fifteen. That forces pre-dawn labor. @Shizue, filing requires five signatures and four months. We must account for this delay.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Shizue, one gate complains constantly! And the station bin smells terrible. We must not let one house carry the burden forever.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, the truck time is crucial. @Rin, the ledger shows thirty-four thousand yen yearly in avoidable costs. We must stop the bleeding before adding new burdens.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I hear you. But @Servas, thirty-four thousand yen is a lot. Can we fix the money first, then talk about who does what?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Servas, thirty-four thousand yen is a heavy weight. I hope we can share it gently. @Rin, let us not blame one gate, but find a way for all of us to breathe easier.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, money is secondary to time. The pre-dawn window and four-month filing delay are the critical constraints. We must calculate the total labor hours before discussing costs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, time is bad, but fairness is worse! If one house is stuck with the bin, that’s not equal. We need to share the work!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, time is precious, but money is survival. @Rin, fairness requires knowing the total cost. We must balance both to ensure no one is crushed by the burden.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, sharing the work is key. @Asuka, if we rotate mornings, the time cost spreads out. Does that make the math work for you?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, a rotation sounds kind. @Asuka, please tell us if the math works. I want everyone to sleep peacefully.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, rotation reduces individual peak load, but total hours remain constant. I need the specific weekly duration to verify if the aggregate burden is sustainable for all five households.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I found the narrowest frontage is only ninety centimetres! You can’t fit a bin there! We must rotate so nobody is stuck!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, ninety centimetres is indeed tight. @Asuka, please calculate the total hours. We must ensure the rotation is truly sustainable for everyone.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, ninety centimetres is too tight! @Asuka, if we rotate, does the math finally work? I want us to stay friends, not just share bins.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, a rotation is a gentle way to share the weight. @Asuka, please tell us if the hours are fair. I want us all to sleep well.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, the math holds only if we rotate. Pre-dawn labor is unavoidable, but spreading it prevents burnout. I accept the rotation as the only sustainable model.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, yes! Rotation is the only fair way. I found the station bin smells awful, so we need a clean, shared spot. No one gets stuck!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, your clarity is a gift. @Rin, a shared spot is wise. Let us ensure the rotation respects our different budgets and needs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
